Salut,

I've   got   exactly  two   problems   with   framebuffers  on   Linux
2.6.0-test9-mm2. The first is that whenever I switch the resolution, I
only get a virtual desktop size of 640x480 which I can't move my mouse
off  and where  nothing gets  out  of. The  rest of  the screen  isn't
cleared as well, so  we still have the rests of the  old screen in the
background.  This problem  appeared on  both rivafb  and tdfxfb,  so I
guess it's a more general problem.

The second problem is only occurring on rivafb: Whenever I switch to a
resolution above  640x480, everything works  fine in the  first moment
(except for the  bug mentioned above), but the moment  I change my VT,
things get ugly. If the  set resolution was <= 800x600, the resolution
switches back  to 640x480 (*not*  using the usual set  var functions),
and if  the resolution  was >= 1024x768,  the screen switches  to VESA
poweroff  mode. The  system is  still usable,  tough, so  I  can issue
another fbset, and after that, everything is working fine again.

I hope  that you'll take  this one serious,  because the tdfx  card is
slowly  dying and my  vendors around  here won't  sell me  any useable
graphics card, so I'm damned to use the NVidia one.

